apps/web/app/fonts/tiempos/

# runtime-generated data (news events + propagation signals). graph.json + the

# that opts out (FALCON_ENGINE_URL=) still writes these; they are that run's
# scratch state, never the seed, so they must not come back as repo churn.
# The handover briefing caches one report per user and session here. It holds
# a reader's positions, so unlike data/insight it must never be tracked.
# Profile photos (main/profile) — a reader's own picture, never tracked.
# Settings → System / Notifications (main/system, main/notifications) — this machine's own choices.
# Development diagnostics (main/diagnostics/model-selftest.ts) write here; per run, never shared.
# stale artifact of the old double-path bug — never commit this


# Packaged build output. `--config.directories.output=release-new` and the
# release-t* verification builds land beside the default dir, so match the
# prefix: these are 100MB-1GB each and must never reach the remote.

# Quant Lab backfilled price series — regenerable via
# `pnpm --filter @meridian/research exec tsx scripts/quantlab-backfill.ts series`
# (~9 MB, one file per ticker). Config, strategies and the live ledger DO stay in git.
# Full backtest reports carry every signal (megabytes, and one more per run).
# The committed index.json keeps the variant history the guards read.

# stray scratch output
y.err.txt

# Extraction eval dataset — rebuilt from the step1 cache with 'pnpm dataset:build'.
# ~11MB of filing text that already lives in the cache; derived, not source.
data/dataset/

